window.KB_BODY[58]={"tsb100165":"<h2>New Alternator and Refrigerant Compressor Belt Guard</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This service/parts announcement introduces a new alternator and refrigerant compressor belt guard for the QST30 industrial engine. Reference Figure 1 below for the configuration of the new guard on the engine.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/17a00004.png\" alt=\"17a00004.png\"></figure><p>Figure 1, Belt Guard Installed</p><p>The affected applications are Komatsu, HD785 and 330M haul trucks <b>only</b>. This change is an improvement in durability over the previous guard. The new style guard includes vibration isolators at the four mounting tabs. Reference Figure 2 for the configuration of the mounting tabs.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/17a00005.png\" alt=\"17a00005.png\"></figure><p>Figure 2, Belt Guard Mounting Tab Locations</p><p>Approximate engine serial number first for the new alternator and refrigerant compressor belt guard is 37181167, built 16DEC97.</p><p>The new alternator and refrigerant compressor belt guard supersedes guard Part Number 3094661.</p><p>The new belt guard, Part Number 4067854 (Figure 2), is content of option number SG5019. The part numbers listed below complete the content of option number SG5019:</p><div class=\"tw\"><table class=\"doc-table\"><thead><tr><th>Part Number</th><th>Description</th><th>Torque Value</th><th>Quantity</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>3034771</td><td>Spacer, mounting</td><td></td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td><a class=\"lnk part\" href=\"#/part/3093744\">3093744</a></td><td>Capscrew, hexagon head</td><td>62 N•m [48 ft-lb]</td><td>3</td></tr><tr><td>3349409</td><td>Isolators, rubber vibration</td><td></td><td>8</td></tr><tr><td><a class=\"lnk part\" href=\"#/part/3410273\">3410273</a></td><td>Spacer, insert</td><td></td><td>4</td></tr><tr><td><a class=\"lnk part\" href=\"#/part/3896408\">3896408</a></td><td>Capscrew, flanged hexagon head</td><td>62 N•m [48 ft-lb]</td><td>1</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p>The alternator and refrigerant compressor belt guard is <b>not</b> sold as an aftermarket kit. The mounting hardware should be ordered separately.</p><p>The belt guard is mounted to the front of the engine using spacers and vibration isolators, as illustrated in Figure 3.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/17a00006.png\" alt=\"17a00006.png\"></figure><p>Figure 3, Spacer and Vibration Isolator Installation</p><div class=\"callout note\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">i</span>Note · Примечание</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>This is a product improvement and is <b>not</b> subject to campaign.</p></div></div>","tsb100166":"<h2>New Cam Follower Shaft Dowel Rings</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Technical Service Bulletin introduces a new ring dowel for the cam follower assemblies of the QST30 engine.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/04a00021.png\" alt=\"04a00021.png\"></figure><p>The affected applications are all QST30 engines made prior to August 16, 2001 and prior to engine serial number 37199919. This change is implemented due to a possible assembly issue with the previous ring dowels. The old dowels were soft enough to mislocate and deform upon initial installation, thus possibly mislocating the cam follower shaft and causing capscrew clamp load problems. No stock of the old dowel is left in factory production, as of September 17, 2001 and the updates to the online catalog and price/parts lists have been made. Please replace all entries of Part Number 3092504, related to the cam follower assemblies, with Part Number <a class=\"lnk part\" href=\"#/part/4067993\">4067993</a> on hard copies of the QST30 Parts Catalogs.</p><p>Engine serial first for the new, hardened dowel rings is 37199919, built August 16, 2001. This new dowel ring, Part Number <a class=\"lnk part\" href=\"#/part/4067993\">4067993</a>, supersedes Part Number 3092504 for the cam follower assemblies <b>only</b>.</p><div class=\"callout note\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">i</span>Note · Примечание</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>This is a product improvement and is <b>not</b> subject to campaign.</p></div></div>","tsb100187":"<h2>ECM No Communication Troubleshooting Tree</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Technical Service Bulletin introduces the ECM - No Communication Troubleshooting Tree.</p>","tsb100242":"<h2>New FS1006 Fuel Filter</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Service Parts Topic introduces the new-style FS1006 fuel filter as the replacement to the old-style FS1006. The new-style fuel filter now incorporates a droptube to help prevent hard start events on some High Horsepower engines due to air in the fuel filters being allowed to flow to the fuel pump.</p><p>There are no external differences in appearance between the old and new-style filters.</p><p>Old and new style filters may be intermixed.</p><p>The old Part Number 3089916, (figure 1), has been made obsolete and supersedes to Part Number <a class=\"lnk part\" href=\"#/part/4095189\">4095189</a> (figure 2).</p><p>A non-droptube version is no longer in production.</p><div class=\"tw\"><table class=\"doc-table\"><thead><tr><th>Old Part Number</th><th>New Part Number</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>3089916</td><td><a class=\"lnk part\" href=\"#/part/4095189\">4095189</a></td></tr></tbody></table></div><div class=\"callout note\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">i</span>Note · Примечание</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>Although the addition of a droptube will greatly reduce, or eliminate, the amount of air going to the fuel pump, the new droptube fuel filter is <b>not</b> a substitute for the Troubleshooting Symptoms Charts. Follow the appropriate Troubleshooting Symptoms Charts available in the Troubleshooting and Repairs Manual.</p></div></div><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/06800007.png\" alt=\"06800007.png\"></figure><p>Figure 1. Non-droptube</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/06800008.png\" alt=\"06800008.png\"></figure><p>Figure 2. With droptube</p><p>This is a product improvement <b>not</b> subject to campaign.</p>","tsb100261":"<h2>Spacer Washer for the Harness Mounting</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Technical Service Bulletin announces the addition of a spacer washer under the two P-clips which support the Bosch® EHAB harness wire and the injector fuel return line. The clips are mounted on the left bank fuel pump mount on QST30 series engines.</p><p>The washer is needed because the fuel pump mount has a recessed spot face which will bend or fracture the bottom P-clip when the capscrew is torqued.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/19a00815.png\" alt=\"19a00815.png\"></figure><p>Figure 1, New Spacer Washer Installed</p><p>The washer, Part Number <a class=\"lnk part\" href=\"#/part/3094024\">3094024</a>, will be added to options PH5723, PH5724 and PH5725.</p><div class=\"callout note\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">i</span>Note · Примечание</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>This is a product improvement <b>not</b> subject to campaign.</p></div></div>","tsb100266":"<h2>Spacer for Turbocharger Oil Supply Line Bracket</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Technical Service Bulletin announces the release of a turbocharger oil supply hose bracket spacer for the QST30 engine. The bracket spacer was implemented to reduce the possibility of contact between the turbocharger oil supply hose and the fuel return tube. The spacer, Part Number <a class=\"lnk part\" href=\"#/part/3092334\">3092334</a>, is placed under the existing oil supply hose bracket mounted to the rocker lever housing. The new spacer requires a longer capscrew, Part Number <a class=\"lnk part\" href=\"#/part/3094813\">3094813</a>, due to the addition of the spacer. This spacer and capscrew are used on both the left and right banks of the engine.</p><p>The illustration below shows the proper installation of the new spacer (1) and capscrew (2).</p><div class=\"callout note\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">i</span>Note · Примечание</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>The illustration shows a portion of the fuel return tube removed for clarity.</p></div></div><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/07a00140.png\" alt=\"07a00140.png\"></figure><p>The new spacer and capscrew have been implemented into production on all QST30 engines starting August 14, 2003, with engine serial number first 37208615.</p><div class=\"callout note\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">i</span>Note · Примечание</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>This is a product improvement <b>not</b> subject to campaign.</p></div></div>","tsb100268":"<h2>New Cam Follower Roller</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Technical Service Bulletin announces the release of a new cam follower roller for the QST30 engine. The new roller has an improved radius across the roller face and an improved hardening process to improve reliability. The new rollers are available individually or as a cam follower lever assembly.</p><div class=\"tw\"><table class=\"doc-table\"><thead><tr><th>Part Number Supercession</th><th></th><th></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Description</td><td>Old Part Number</td><td>New Part Number</td></tr><tr><td>Cam Roller</td><td>4068231</td><td><a class=\"lnk part\" href=\"#/part/4068548\">4068548</a></td></tr><tr><td>Lever assembly</td><td>3092499</td><td><a class=\"lnk part\" href=\"#/part/4068611\">4068611</a></td></tr></tbody></table></div><p>There are no markings or visible differences between the old and new rollers. The new cam follower roller was implemented into production on September 24, 2003 with engine serial number first of 37209159.</p><p>Cummins Inc. recommends installing these new rollers and pins in place of old components during engine rebuild.</p><div class=\"callout note\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">i</span>Note · Примечание</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>This is a product improvement <b>not</b> subject to campaign.</p></div></div>","tsb100362":"<h2>Fuel Line Bracket</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Technical Service Bulletin announces an additional bracket to be placed on the right bank cylinder number 3 fuel line. Due to a large unbracketed span of the fuel line, the fuel line was able to vibrate and some have cracked due to high cycle fatigue.</p><p>The bracket components used have the same part numbers used on other fuel lines. No new components were needed or released. The parts will be added in production and are available to order for upfit.</p><div class=\"callout note\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">i</span>Note · Примечание</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>This is a product improvement and is <b>not</b> subject to campaign.</p></div></div><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/06a00124.png\" alt=\"06a00124.png\"></figure><p>The bracket components are listed below:</p><div class=\"tw\"><table class=\"doc-table\"><thead><tr><th>Table 1, Fuel Line Bracket Components</th><th></th><th></th><th></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Item Number</td><td>Part Number</td><td>Description</td><td>Quantity</td></tr><tr><td>1</td><td>*<a class=\"lnk part\" href=\"#/part/3093764\">3093764</a></td><td>Capscrew, hexagon head</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td>2</td><td>68368B</td><td>Spacer, mounting</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td>3</td><td><a class=\"lnk part\" href=\"#/part/4068681\">4068681</a></td><td>Bracket, fuel plumbing</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td>4</td><td><a class=\"lnk part\" href=\"#/part/3092334\">3092334</a></td><td>Spacer, mounting</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td>5</td><td><a class=\"lnk part\" href=\"#/part/3093687\">3093687</a></td><td>Bracket, fuel plumbing</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td>6</td><td><a class=\"lnk part\" href=\"#/part/3093734\">3093734</a></td><td>Capscrew, hexagon head</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td>7</td><td><a class=\"lnk part\" href=\"#/part/3093624\">3093624</a></td><td>Clamp, tube</td><td>2</td></tr></tbody></table></div><div class=\"tw\"><table class=\"doc-table\"><thead><tr><th>*Remove existing part number:</th><th></th><th></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><a class=\"lnk part\" href=\"#/part/3094813\">3094813</a></td><td>Capscrew, hexagon head flange (from rocker lever box location). This screw is replaced with part number <a class=\"lnk part\" href=\"#/part/3093764\">3093764</a>.</td><td>1</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p>The Engine Serial Number (ESN) first for the additional bracket being installed in production is 37216997. The first build date was April 11, 2005.</p><p>There are no changes to the installation and removal procedures.</p>","tsb100369":"<h2>New Gallery Cooled Pistons</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Technical Service Bulletin is to introduce a new galley cooled piston for certain K38-M and K50-M applications. The improved piston is designed to address the failures seen in the bowl rim area of the piston which have been attributed to excessive cylinder temperatures. Contributing factors are exhaust leaks, plugged aftercoolers, and plugged air cleaners.</p><p>The new piston is, Part Number 4097889. The old piston, Part Number 3628731, will still be used on industrial and power generation applications and therefore will <b>not</b> be made obsolete. Both piston Part Number 4097889 and piston Part Number 3628731, are interchangeable, so that single cylinder repairs are possible with the new piston on engines currently in the field. There is no calibration change associated with the new piston.</p><p>The new gallery piston kit is, Part Number 4090013.</p><div class=\"callout note\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">i</span>Note · Примечание</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>Piston, Part Number 4097889, is <b>not</b> interchangeable with spray cooled pistons.</p></div></div><p>The new gallery cooled piston will be available for service orders in March 2005.</p><p>The engine serial number (ESN) first for the new piston is 33160766, built July 04, 2005.</p><p>It is recommended that the new gallery cooled pistons are installed during rebuilds.</p><div class=\"tw\"><table class=\"doc-table\"><thead><tr><th>New Piston Part Numbers</th><th></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Piston Part Number</td><td>4097889</td></tr><tr><td>Piston Kit Part Number</td><td>4090013</td></tr></tbody></table></div><div class=\"tw\"><table class=\"doc-table\"><thead><tr><th>Affected Engines</th><th></th><th></th><th></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Engine</td><td>CPL</td><td>Options</td><td>Option Notes</td></tr><tr><td>KTA38-M2 and KTA38-D(M1)</td><td>2404</td><td>PP 6741</td><td>Non-certified piston and rod</td></tr><tr><td>2404</td><td>PP 6742</td><td>Agency approved piston and rod</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>KTA50-M2 and KTA50-D(M1)</td><td>8063</td><td>PP 6724</td><td>Non-certified piston and rod</td></tr><tr><td>2589</td><td>PP 6730</td><td>Agency approved piston and rod</td><td></td></tr></tbody></table></div><div class=\"callout note\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">i</span>Note · Примечание</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>This is a product improvement and <b>not</b> subject to campaign.</p></div></div>","tsb100373":"<h2>Electric Fuel Lift Pump Improvement</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Technical Service Bulletin informs the field of a part number change due to improvements made to the electric fuel lift pump used on QST30 Power Generation and some industrial products. The old fuel lift pump, Part Number 4067830, has been obsoleted. The new fuel lift pump, Part Number 4295249, is now available and has been installed on engines starting with Engine Serial Number First 37215814, built on January 31, 2005.</p><p>To attain the maximum reliability improvement, do <b>not</b> mix old and new pumps.</p><p>In accordance with Application Engineering Bulletin 70.30, 140 micron pre-filtration is required for all QST30 engines with electric lift pumps. Engines built since May of 2004 include a 140 micron prefilter. Option FS5033 is an available 140 micron prefilter option.</p><div class=\"callout note\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">i</span>Note · Примечание</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>This is a product improvement and is <b>not</b> subject to campaign.</p></div></div>","tsb100383":"<h2>New High Horsepower Machined-from-Solid Turbocharger Compressor Wheel</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Technical Service Bulletin announces a new machined-from-solid turbocharger compressor wheel for QST30 engines operating in specific applications. The new turbocharger was released to resolve low-cycle fatigue issues.</p><p>The previous compressor wheel is cast with the outer blade contour machined to achieve the desired profile. The sides of the cast wheel blades are left in the &#x27;as cast&#x27; condition.</p><p>The new compressor wheel is machined from a solid billet of aluminum to reduce the number of inclusions in the wheel. All surfaces of the machined-from-solid wheel are machined.</p><p>This product improvement is <b>not</b> covered by warranty.</p><p><b>Only</b> certain, high-duty cycle applications require the use of turbochargers with machined-from-solid turbocharger compressor wheels.</p><p>Consult QuickServe® Online to determine if a given engine and application combination is eligible to receive this product improvement.</p><div class=\"callout note\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">i</span>Note · Примечание</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>This is a product improvement and is <b>not</b> subject to campaign.</p></div></div><p>The compatibility chart below shows the machined-from-solid turbocharger compressor wheel that can potentially be used with the CPL listed.</p><div class=\"tw\"><table class=\"doc-table\"><thead><tr><th>Engine</th><th>New CPL</th><th>Old CPL</th><th>Turbocharger with Cast Compressor Wheels</th><th>Turbocharger with MFS Compressor Wheels</th><th>MFS Service Kit</th><th>MFS ReCon®</th><th>Direct Supersession?</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>QST30</td><td>0191</td><td>2640</td><td>3592968</td><td>4039206</td><td>4090019</td><td>N/A</td><td>Yes</td></tr></tbody></table></div>","tsb100433":"<h2>Two Stage Frame Identification</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This document informs the field of the changes made to two stage frames during design changes from initial product introduction to current production frames.</p><p>From initial introduction of the two stage frame there has been a total of eight changes in part number allocated to the mounting frame.</p><p>This document will give both a visual and a descriptive listing to identify which part number is the allocated frame.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/10600476.png\" alt=\"10600476.png\"></figure><p>Figure 1, Frame, Part Number 3411156</p><p>Frame, Part Number 3411156:</p><p>Initial frame design released for production two stage engines. The original &quot;twin deck&quot; frame with exhaust outlets mounted on plates above the high pressure turbochargers.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/10600477.png\" alt=\"10600477.png\"></figure><p>Figure 2, Frame, Part Number 4016774</p><p>Frame, Part Number 4016774:</p><p>Re-designed to introduce mounting the exhaust outlet pads to the &quot;I&quot; beam section with no cross braces.</p><p>A - Exhaust outlet mounting pads attached to center &quot;I&quot; beam only.</p><p>B - Central exhaust outlet mount is a two piece component.</p><p>C - Capped end, semi-circular load spreaders.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/10600478.png\" alt=\"10600478.png\"></figure><p>Figure 3, Frame, Part Number 4100475</p><p>Frame, Part Number 4100475:</p><p>A - Un-capped box section load spreaders.</p><p>B - Late frames have holes added for coolant loop mounting.</p><div class=\"callout note\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">i</span>Note · Примечание</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>Early frames did <b>not</b> include holes for the coolant loop tubing. Later frames will have holes included.</p></div></div><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/10600479.png\" alt=\"10600479.png\"></figure><p>Figure 4, Frame, Part Number 4101183</p><p>Frame, Part Number 4101183:</p><p>As frame number 4100475, except for:</p><p>A - Two tapped holes in center turbocharger mount support gusset</p><p>B - Two tapped holes in rear channel cross member.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/10600480.png\" alt=\"10600480.png\"></figure><p>Figure 5, Frame, Part Number 3635285</p><p>Frame, Part Number 3635285:</p><p>As frame number 4101183, except center &quot;I&quot; beam is constructed by two pressed steel sections welded together &#x27;A&#x27;.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/10r00145.png\" alt=\"10r00145.png\"></figure><p>Figure 6, Frame, Part Number 3635903</p><p>Frame, Part Number 3635903:</p><p>As frame number 3635285 except for modified and added side rail holes positions.</p><p>This frame is known as Tier 1 framework.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/10r00146.png\" alt=\"10r00146.png\"></figure><p>Figure 7, Frame, Part Number 4927515</p><p>Frame, Part Number 4927515:</p><p>As frame number 3635903 except:</p><ul><li>The addition of side rail break to avoid contact with high pressure turbocharger re-orientation (A)</li><li>The addition of tabs at load spreaders (B)</li><li>Modified side rail holes positions (C)</li><li>Removed pads (D)</li></ul><p>This frame is known as initial Tier 2 framework.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/10r00147.png\" alt=\"10r00147.png\"></figure><p>Figure 8, Frame, Part Number 3642933</p><p>Frame, Part Number 3642933:</p><p>Existing frame that is known as common framework for Tier 1 and Tier 2.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/10r00148.png\" alt=\"10r00148.png\"></figure><p>Figure 9, Two Stage Frame Identification Matrix</p><h3>Document History</h3>","tsb100441":"<h2>QST30 Tier 2 Engine Introduction</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><div class=\"callout note\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">i</span>Note · Примечание</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>This Technical Service Bulletin supersedes and replaces Service/Parts Topics 97t0-7 and 99t0-22.</p></div></div><p>This Technical Service Bulletin announces the introduction of the QST30 Tier 2, Tier 1, non-certified products, and identifies unique engine components for the non-certified products.</p><p>The QST30 Tier 2 engine is redesigned to address the US Environmental Protection Agency (EPA) exhaust emissions levels for off-highway engines in the &gt;560 kW [&gt;751 HP] power category built after 01 January 2006. It is built to meet and exceed present and future competitive pressures, worldwide emissions regulations, and corporate standards for performance, reliability and durability.</p><div class=\"tw\"><table class=\"doc-table\"><thead><tr><th>QST30 Tier 2 Industrial</th><th></th><th></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Configuration Number</td><td>D573002CX03</td><td>D573003CX03</td></tr><tr><td>Number of Cylinders</td><td>12</td><td>12</td></tr><tr><td>Displacement</td><td>30.5 liters [1860 in 3 ]</td><td>30.5 liters [1861 in 3 ]</td></tr><tr><td>Bore</td><td>140 mm [5.51 in]</td><td>140 mm [5.51 in]</td></tr><tr><td>Stroke</td><td>165 mm [6.5 in]</td><td>165 mm [6.5 in]</td></tr><tr><td>Compression Ratio</td><td>15.7:1</td><td>14.7:1</td></tr><tr><td>Aspiration</td><td>Turbocharged and Charge Air Cooled</td><td>Turbocharged and 2-Pump 2-Loop Aftercooled</td></tr><tr><td>Approximate Engine Weight</td><td>3328 kg [7337 lbs]</td><td>3328 kg [7337 lbs]</td></tr><tr><td>Maximum Overspeed Capacity</td><td>2625 rpm</td><td>2625 rpm</td></tr></tbody></table></div><div class=\"tw\"><table class=\"doc-table\"><thead><tr><th>QST30 Tier 2 Power Generation</th><th></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Configuration Number</td><td>D573001GX03</td></tr><tr><td>Number of Cylinders</td><td>12</td></tr><tr><td>Displacement</td><td>30.5 liters [1860 in 3 ]</td></tr><tr><td>Bore</td><td>140 mm [5.51 in]</td></tr><tr><td>Stroke</td><td>165 mm [6.5 in]</td></tr><tr><td>Compression Ratio</td><td>14.7:1</td></tr><tr><td>Aspiration</td><td>Turbocharged and Charge Air Cooled, 2-Pump 2-Loop Aftercooled, Jacket Water Aftercooled</td></tr><tr><td>Approximate Engine Weight</td><td>3112 kg [6860 lbs]</td></tr><tr><td>Maximum Overspeed Capacity</td><td>2625 rpm</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p>QST30 Tier 2 Engine Ratings (Industrial)</p><p>The fuel ratings available for the QST30 Tier 2 engine are essentially a carryover from the QST30 Tier 1 engine. The performance parts have been developed to meet Tier 2 emission levels, achieve the best possible fuel consumption, and achieve similar transient response as the Tier 1 engine.</p><p>The Tier 2 ratings shown below are planned for production availability. Additional ratings, performance curves, and data sheets are available and can be obtained at a Cummins Authorized Service Location.</p><div class=\"tw\"><table class=\"doc-table\"><thead><tr><th>QST30 Configuration Number - D573002CX03</th><th></th><th></th><th></th><th></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Option Number</td><td>CPL Number</td><td>Power kW [bhp] @ rpm</td><td>Peak Torque N•m [ft-lb] @ rpm</td><td>Rating Type</td></tr><tr><td>FR 5234</td><td>1244</td><td>895 [1200] @ 2100</td><td>5084 [3750] @ 1400</td><td>Restricted</td></tr><tr><td>FR 5235</td><td>1244</td><td>895 [1200] @ 1900</td><td>5085 [3751] @ 1400</td><td>Restricted</td></tr><tr><td>FR 5236</td><td>1244</td><td>820 [1100] @ 2100</td><td>4629 [3414] @ 1400</td><td>Intermittent</td></tr><tr><td>FR 5237</td><td>1244</td><td>783 [1050] @ 2100</td><td>4629 [3414] @ 1300</td><td>Intermittent</td></tr><tr><td>FR 5239</td><td>1244</td><td>783 [1050] @ 1900</td><td>4629 [3414] @ 1300</td><td>Intermittent</td></tr><tr><td>FR 5238</td><td>1244</td><td>783 [1050] @ 1800</td><td>4629 [3414] @ 1300</td><td>Intermittent</td></tr><tr><td>FR 5240</td><td>1244</td><td>746 [1000] @ 2100</td><td>4629 [3414] @ 1300</td><td>Intermittent</td></tr><tr><td>FR 5241</td><td>1244</td><td>746 [1000] @ 1800</td><td>4629 [3414] @ 1300</td><td>Intermittent</td></tr><tr><td>FR 5242</td><td>1244</td><td>708 [950] @ 2100</td><td>4188 [3089] @ 1300</td><td>Intermittent</td></tr><tr><td>FR 5243</td><td>1244</td><td>671 [900] @ 2100</td><td>3747 [2764] @ 1300</td><td>Intermittent</td></tr><tr><td>FR 5244</td><td>1244</td><td>634 [850] @ 2000</td><td>3806 [2807] @ 1400</td><td>Intermittent</td></tr><tr><td>FR 5245</td><td>1244</td><td>634 [850] @ 1800</td><td>3806 [2807] @ 1400</td><td>Continuous</td></tr><tr><td>FR 5246</td><td>1244</td><td>567 [760] @ 2100</td><td>3350 [2471] @ 1300</td><td>Intermittent</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p>Engine Ratings (Power Generation)</p><p>The fuel ratings available for the QST30 Tier 2 engine are essentially a carryover from the QST30 Tier 1 engine. The performance parts have been developed to meet Tier 2 emission levels, achieve the best possible fuel consumption, and achieve similar transient response as the Tier 1 engine. The QST30 Tier 2 ratings shown in the table below are planned for production availability. Additional ratings can be requested by submitting a Value Package Change Request (VPCR). Additional ratings, performance curves, and data sheets are available and can be obtained at a Cummins Authorized Service Location.</p><div class=\"tw\"><table class=\"doc-table\"><thead><tr><th></th><th></th><th>Standby</th><th>Prime</th><th>Continuous</th><th>Cooling</th><th></th><th></th><th></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td></td><td></td><td>1500</td><td>1800</td><td>1500</td><td>1800</td><td>1500</td><td>1800</td><td></td></tr><tr><td></td><td></td><td>HP/KWm</td><td>HP/KWm</td><td>HP/KWm</td><td>HP/KWm</td><td>HP/KWm</td><td>HP/KWm</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>FR 5247</td><td>QST30-G5 NR2</td><td>N/A</td><td>1490/1112</td><td>N/A</td><td>1350/1007</td><td>N/A</td><td>1115/832</td><td>2P2L</td></tr><tr><td>FR 5250</td><td>QST30-G5 NR2</td><td>N/A</td><td>1490/1112</td><td>N/A</td><td>1350/1007</td><td>N/A</td><td>1115/832</td><td>ATA</td></tr><tr><td>Additional ratings, performance curves, and data sheets are available and can be obtained at a Cummins Authorized Service Location.</td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr></tbody></table></div><p>The QST30 Industrial Tier 1 service parts topic introduced the Tier 1 emission-certified QST30 engine for mobile off-highway applications. A new procedure for the charge-air cooler (CAC), a new symptom tree, and revisions to five other symptom trees were also included in the Tier 1 engine introduction.</p><p>To meet year 2000 Environmental Protection Agency (EPA) and California Air Resources Board (CARB) Tier 1 emission levels, it was necessary to change the non-certified QST30 aspiration from turbocharged and jacket water aftercooled (JWAC) to turbocharged and charge-air cooled (CAC). The Tier 1 product employs two separate cooling circuits; A liquid-coolant-filled high-temperature circuit (HTC) for the main engine jacket water cooling, and a low-temperature, air-to-air circuit (LTC) for charge-air cooling. This topic addressed <b>only</b> the differences between the Tier 1 and non-certified QST30 Industrial engines.</p><p>Charge-air cooling of the intake air was required to retain engine efficiency while injection timing was retarded to obtain lower NOx. Charge-air cooling also allowed higher horsepower capabilities for the equivalent thermal loading. In addition to the non-certified QST30 power ranges of 760 hp to 1050 hp, a 1200 hp with 6000-foot altitude capability became available. The new offering also featured a 25 percent torque rise and is restricted to intermittent applications with load factors equal to or less than 40 percent.</p><p>QST30 Industrial Tier 1 limited production began 01 January 2000 and retained the configuration number D573002CX03.</p><p>For general charge-air cooling installation guidelines, see the Application Engineering Bulletin Number 3884966, (AEB) 24.06 - 1999 Industrial Application Installation Recommendations, Charge-Air Cooling.</p><p>Emission Regulations</p><div class=\"tw\"><table class=\"doc-table\"><thead><tr><th>Year 2000 Tier 1 Emission Regulations</th><th></th><th></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Emission Regulating Agency</td><td>Emission Limit (g/bhp-hr) NOx</td><td>Horsepower</td></tr><tr><td>CARB</td><td>6.9 NOx</td><td>Above 750 hp</td></tr><tr><td>EPA</td><td>6.9 NOx</td><td>Above 750 hp</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p>Ratings</p><div class=\"callout note\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">i</span>Note · Примечание</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>The <b>only</b> difference between CPL 2640 and CPL 2818 is the orientation of the turbocharger compressor housings. The base turbocharger part number is the same for the two CPLs.</p></div></div><div class=\"tw\"><table class=\"doc-table\"><thead><tr><th>QST30 Industrial Tier 1 Ratings</th><th></th><th></th><th></th><th></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Engine Model</td><td>Rated Horsepower kW [bhp] rpm, N•m [ft-lb] rpm</td><td>Application</td><td>CPL</td><td>ECM Code</td></tr><tr><td>QST30-C</td><td>669 [897]@2000 rpm. Torque peak: 4103 [3026]@1300 rpm</td><td>Komatsu WA900, front-out exhaust</td><td>2640</td><td>K50017</td></tr><tr><td>QST30-C</td><td>807 [897]@2000 rpm. Torque peak: 4629 [3414]@1400 rpm</td><td>Komatsu 330M, rear-out exhaust, with PMC, with CENSE™</td><td>2818</td><td>K50019</td></tr><tr><td>QST30-C</td><td>567 [760]@2100 rpm. Torque peak: 3350 [2471]@1300 rpm</td><td>Kawasaki 135Z</td><td>2640</td><td>K50018</td></tr><tr><td>Additional ratings, performance curves, and data sheets are available and can be obtained at a Cummins Authorized Service Location.</td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr></tbody></table></div><p>The QST30-C Industrial service parts topic announced the introduction of the QST30-C Industrial engine.</p><p>New industrial ratings of the QST30 engine were released for limited production in September, 1997. Four ratings of this industrial engine were released. The QST30-C uses many of the successfully proven technologies already in production on QST30 Power Generation engines. The QST30-C uses a full-authority electronic Bosch® fuel system, Cummins Inc. developed controls, and is fully compatible with the CENSE™ engine monitoring system. QST30-C Industrial ratings are designed to replace V28 and lower K38 ratings with improved fuel economy, transient response, emissions, and diagnostic capabilities.</p><div class=\"tw\"><table class=\"doc-table\"><thead><tr><th>QST30-C Non-Certified Industrial</th><th></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Model Name</td><td>QST30-1050</td></tr><tr><td>Configuration Number</td><td>D573002CX03</td></tr><tr><td>CPL</td><td>2127</td></tr><tr><td>Fuel Code</td><td>105</td></tr><tr><td>Injector (Qty.)</td><td>3092022 (2), 3092023 (10)</td></tr><tr><td>Crankshaft</td><td><a class=\"lnk part\" href=\"#/part/3092922\">3092922</a></td></tr><tr><td>Camshft (Qty.)</td><td><a class=\"lnk part\" href=\"#/part/3092971\">3092971</a> (1), <a class=\"lnk part\" href=\"#/part/3092974\">3092974</a> (1).</td></tr><tr><td>Piston (Qty.)</td><td>3092606 (6), 3092607, (6).</td></tr><tr><td>Turbocharger (Qty.)</td><td>3537114 (1), 3097115 (1).</td></tr><tr><td>Cylinder Head</td><td>3094190</td></tr><tr><td>Horsepower</td><td>1050 hp @ 2100 rpm</td></tr><tr><td>Torque</td><td>3415 ft-lb @ 1300 rpm</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p>The QST30-C Industrial engine contains several unique parts. A general description of these components and a listing of parts that are not shared with the power generation QST30 engines. Components are organized by group for ease of use.</p><div class=\"callout note\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">i</span>Note · Примечание</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>The QST30-C engines used in Komatsu applications will be Komatsu branded and designated SA12V140 Z-1. They will <b>not</b> be Cummins Inc. labeled or identified as QST30-C. The engines in Komatsu applications are <b>not</b> covered by Cummins Inc. warranty, and they will be serviced through the Komatsu service network.</p></div></div>","tsb100490":"<h2>Water Pump Coolant Seal, Material Change</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Technical Service Bulletin is to inform the field of a new and improved water pump coolant seal, Part Number <a class=\"lnk part\" href=\"#/part/4096426\">4096426</a>. The new water pump coolant seal incorporates a higher temperature rubber material and is designed to improve the water pump sealing durability. The new water pump coolant seal replaces the old water pump coolant seal, Part Number 3092348. Production use began with engine serial number (ESN) first 37223634.</p><p>The new water pump coolant seal is included in the following water pumps and water pump repair kits:</p><div class=\"tw\"><table class=\"doc-table\"><thead><tr><th>Table 1, Water Pumps and Water Pump Repair Kits</th><th></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Part Number</td><td>Description</td></tr><tr><td><a class=\"lnk part\" href=\"#/part/4090032\">4090032</a></td><td>Water pump repair (minor)</td></tr><tr><td>4090033</td><td>Water pump repair (major)</td></tr><tr><td><a class=\"lnk part\" href=\"#/part/4090034\">4090034</a></td><td>Water pump repair</td></tr><tr><td><a class=\"lnk part\" href=\"#/part/4096427\">4096427</a></td><td>Water pump</td></tr><tr><td>4096429</td><td>Water pump</td></tr></tbody></table></div><div class=\"callout note\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">i</span>Note · Примечание</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>This is a product improvement and is <b>not</b> subject to campaign.</p></div></div>","tsb100524":"<h2>Revised Exhaust Manifold Part Numbers</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Technical Service Bulletin lists which exhaust manifold part numbers are required for each manifold configuration on QST30 engines. The manifold part numbers are categorized by exhaust manifold option (TBXXXX) and by front out or rear out exhaust configurations.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/14a00016.png\" alt=\"14a00016.png\"></figure><ol><li>Pipe plug</li><li>Pipe plug</li><li>Exhaust manifold</li><li>Exhaust manifold</li><li>Exhaust manifold</li><li>Exhaust manifold</li><li>Stud</li><li>Exhaust manifold gasket</li><li>Turbocharger gasket</li><li>Mounting spacer</li><li>Hex head capscrew.</li></ol><div class=\"tw\"><table class=\"doc-table\"><thead><tr><th>Front Out Exhaust Manifold Configurations</th><th></th><th></th><th></th><th></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Exhaust Manifold Option</td><td>Bank</td><td>Front</td><td>Center</td><td>Rear</td></tr><tr><td>TB5712</td><td>Left</td><td><a class=\"lnk part\" href=\"#/part/3092658\">3092658</a></td><td>3092659</td><td><a class=\"lnk part\" href=\"#/part/3092657\">3092657</a></td></tr><tr><td>Right</td><td><a class=\"lnk part\" href=\"#/part/3092657\">3092657</a></td><td>3092660</td><td><a class=\"lnk part\" href=\"#/part/3092658\">3092658</a></td><td></td></tr><tr><td>TB5713</td><td>Left</td><td>3092062</td><td>3092063</td><td>2092061</td></tr><tr><td>Right</td><td>3092061</td><td>3092064</td><td>3092062</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>TB5718</td><td>Left</td><td><a class=\"lnk part\" href=\"#/part/3092658\">3092658</a></td><td>3092534</td><td><a class=\"lnk part\" href=\"#/part/3092657\">3092657</a></td></tr><tr><td>Right</td><td><a class=\"lnk part\" href=\"#/part/3092657\">3092657</a></td><td>3092533</td><td><a class=\"lnk part\" href=\"#/part/3092658\">3092658</a></td><td></td></tr><tr><td>TB5722</td><td>Left</td><td>3092062</td><td>4067920</td><td>3092061</td></tr><tr><td>Right</td><td>3092061</td><td>4067921</td><td>3092062</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>TB5728</td><td>Left</td><td><a class=\"lnk part\" href=\"#/part/3092658\">3092658</a></td><td>3092534</td><td><a class=\"lnk part\" href=\"#/part/3092657\">3092657</a></td></tr><tr><td>Right</td><td><a class=\"lnk part\" href=\"#/part/3092657\">3092657</a></td><td>3092533</td><td><a class=\"lnk part\" href=\"#/part/3092658\">3092658</a></td><td></td></tr><tr><td>TB5730</td><td>Left</td><td>3092062</td><td>4067920</td><td>3092061</td></tr><tr><td>Right</td><td>3092061</td><td>4067921</td><td>3092062</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>TB5732</td><td>Left</td><td><a class=\"lnk part\" href=\"#/part/3092658\">3092658</a></td><td><a class=\"lnk part\" href=\"#/part/4295291\">4295291</a></td><td><a class=\"lnk part\" href=\"#/part/3092657\">3092657</a></td></tr><tr><td>Right</td><td><a class=\"lnk part\" href=\"#/part/3092657\">3092657</a></td><td><a class=\"lnk part\" href=\"#/part/4295293\">4295293</a></td><td><a class=\"lnk part\" href=\"#/part/3092658\">3092658</a></td><td></td></tr><tr><td>TB5733</td><td>Left</td><td>3092062</td><td>4295454</td><td>3092061</td></tr><tr><td>Right</td><td>3092061</td><td>4295456</td><td>3092062</td><td></td></tr></tbody></table></div><div class=\"tw\"><table class=\"doc-table\"><thead><tr><th>Rear Out Exhaust Manifold Configurations</th><th></th><th></th><th></th><th></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Exhaust Manifold Option</td><td>Bank</td><td>Front</td><td>Center</td><td>Rear</td></tr><tr><td>TB5712</td><td>Left</td><td><a class=\"lnk part\" href=\"#/part/3092658\">3092658</a></td><td>3092660</td><td><a class=\"lnk part\" href=\"#/part/3092657\">3092657</a></td></tr><tr><td>Right</td><td><a class=\"lnk part\" href=\"#/part/3092657\">3092657</a></td><td>3092659</td><td><a class=\"lnk part\" href=\"#/part/3092658\">3092658</a></td><td></td></tr><tr><td>TB5713</td><td>Left</td><td>3092062</td><td>3092064</td><td>2092061</td></tr><tr><td>Right</td><td>3092061</td><td>3092063</td><td>3092062</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>TB5718</td><td>Left</td><td><a class=\"lnk part\" href=\"#/part/3092658\">3092658</a></td><td>3092533</td><td><a class=\"lnk part\" href=\"#/part/3092657\">3092657</a></td></tr><tr><td>Right</td><td><a class=\"lnk part\" href=\"#/part/3092657\">3092657</a></td><td>3092534</td><td><a class=\"lnk part\" href=\"#/part/3092658\">3092658</a></td><td></td></tr><tr><td>TB5722</td><td>Left</td><td>3092062</td><td>4067921</td><td>3092061</td></tr><tr><td>Right</td><td>3092061</td><td>4067920</td><td>3092062</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>TB5728</td><td>Left</td><td><a class=\"lnk part\" href=\"#/part/3092658\">3092658</a></td><td>3092533</td><td><a class=\"lnk part\" href=\"#/part/3092657\">3092657</a></td></tr><tr><td>Right</td><td><a class=\"lnk part\" href=\"#/part/3092657\">3092657</a></td><td>3092534</td><td><a class=\"lnk part\" href=\"#/part/3092658\">3092658</a></td><td></td></tr><tr><td>TB5730</td><td>Left</td><td>3092062</td><td>4067921</td><td>3092061</td></tr><tr><td>Right</td><td>3092061</td><td>4067920</td><td>3092062</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>TB5732</td><td>Left</td><td><a class=\"lnk part\" href=\"#/part/3092658\">3092658</a></td><td><a class=\"lnk part\" href=\"#/part/4295293\">4295293</a></td><td><a class=\"lnk part\" href=\"#/part/3092657\">3092657</a></td></tr><tr><td>Right</td><td><a class=\"lnk part\" href=\"#/part/3092657\">3092657</a></td><td><a class=\"lnk part\" href=\"#/part/4295291\">4295291</a></td><td><a class=\"lnk part\" href=\"#/part/3092658\">3092658</a></td><td></td></tr><tr><td>TB5733</td><td>Left</td><td>3092062</td><td>4295456</td><td>3092061</td></tr><tr><td>Right</td><td>3092061</td><td>4295454</td><td>3092062</td><td></td></tr></tbody></table></div>","tsb100542":"<h2>New Fuel Shutoff Valve</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Technical Service Bulletin introduces a new fuel shutoff valve and all the associated parts that are now available for the QST30 engine (all applications).</p><p>The new fuel shutoff valve features the following product improvements:</p><ul><li>modified wear plate designed to conform with other high horsepower engine families</li><li>modified fuel manifold counter bore depth to adjust for wear plate</li><li>new actuator disc for improved flow characteristics.</li></ul><p>The engine serial number (ESN) first for the new fuel shutoff valve is 37226082 and occurred on November 1, 2006.</p><p>The new fuel manifold assembly obsoletes and supersedes the old fuel manifold assembly.</p><div class=\"tw\"><table class=\"doc-table\"><thead><tr><th>New and Old Fuel Shutoff Valve Part Numbers</th><th></th><th></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Description</td><td>Old Part Number</td><td>New Part Number</td></tr><tr><td>Assembly, fuel manifold</td><td>3093521</td><td>4295494</td></tr><tr><td>- Spring, valve</td><td>- 129768</td><td>- 129768</td></tr><tr><td>- Housing, actuator</td><td>- Not applicable</td><td>- <a class=\"lnk part\" href=\"#/part/4088863\">4088863</a></td></tr><tr><td>- Shield, shutoff valve</td><td>- 129839</td><td>- 129839</td></tr><tr><td>- Screw, captive washer</td><td>- Not applicable</td><td>- <a class=\"lnk part\" href=\"#/part/3065944\">3065944</a></td></tr><tr><td>- Disc, valve</td><td>- 196057</td><td>- 196057</td></tr><tr><td>- Solenoid</td><td>- <a class=\"lnk part\" href=\"#/part/3021420\">3021420</a></td><td>- <a class=\"lnk part\" href=\"#/part/3021420\">3021420</a></td></tr><tr><td>- Disc, actuator</td><td>- <a class=\"lnk part\" href=\"#/part/3056009\">3056009</a></td><td>- <a class=\"lnk part\" href=\"#/part/4088274\">4088274</a></td></tr><tr><td>- Seal, rectangular ring</td><td>- 3094667</td><td>- 3094667</td></tr><tr><td>- Seal, rectangular ring</td><td>- Not applicable</td><td>- 129888</td></tr></tbody></table></div><div class=\"callout note\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">i</span>Note · Примечание</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>This is a product improvement and is <b>not</b> subject to campaign.</p></div></div>","tsb100564":"<h2>New One Piece Wiring Harness with Electric Lift Pump Logic</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Technical Service Bulletin introduces a new one piece wiring harness and fuel extension harness that are available for all QST30 engine applications that use an electric fuel lift pump. The new one piece harness utilizes an additional oil temperature sensor breakout for an optional sensor on the left bank front oil port. The new harness is grounded through the ECM connection so it does <b>not</b> require a ground connection to the engine block.</p><p>The new part was introduced with Engine Serial Number (ESN) first 37226833 on January 30, 2007.</p><p>New sensor part numbers, shown below, are required with the implementation of the new one piece wiring harness and fuel system extension harness.</p><div class=\"tw\"><table class=\"doc-table\"><thead><tr><th>Old Part Number</th><th>Quantity</th><th>New Part Number</th><th>Description</th><th>Location</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>3093261, 3093363, 3658785</td><td>1</td><td>4067866</td><td>Harness, ETR CNT MDL WRG (One Piece Harness)</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>4068024</td><td>1</td><td>4295539</td><td>Harness, Wiring (Fuel System Extension Harness)</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>3408589</td><td>2</td><td>3408556</td><td>Sensor, Pressure (Right Bank and Left Bank Intake Manifold Pressure)</td><td>Left Bank and Right Bank Intake Manifolds</td></tr><tr><td>3408587</td><td>1</td><td>3408560</td><td>Sensor, Pressure (Oil Pressure)</td><td>Left Bank, Middle Port on Oil Rifle</td></tr><tr><td>N/A</td><td>1</td><td>3865346</td><td>Sensor, Temperature (Oil Temperature)</td><td>Left Bank, Front Port on Oil Rifle</td></tr><tr><td>N/A</td><td>8</td><td>4295622</td><td>Grommet</td><td>ECM Connector Cover</td></tr></tbody></table></div>","tsb100575":"<h2>New Intake Valves</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This document introduces new intake valves for the K38, K50, QSK45 and QSK60 series engines manufactured at the Daventry Engine Plant. The new intake valves utilize a nitride hardening process known as Sursulf. The benefits of Sursulf are:</p><ul><li>Increased surface hardness</li><li>Increased fatigue strength</li><li>Improved wear resistance.</li></ul><p>Sursulf valves can <b>not</b> be ground. Grinding will remove a significant portion of the hardened layer. Ground valves will be susceptible to &#x27;beat in&#x27; wear and premature failure.</p><p>It is <b>not</b> recommended to intermix old intake valve part numbers with the new Sursulf valve part numbers in the same cylinder head. Cylinder head combinations are acceptable on the same engine.</p><p>The new valves have a darker appearance when compared to the old design; other markings are described below.</p><div class=\"callout note\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">i</span>Note · Примечание</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>Engines manufactured at Cummins® India Ltd. continue to use the old valve part numbers.</p></div></div><div class=\"tw\"><table class=\"doc-table\"><thead><tr><th>Intake Valve Part Numbers*</th><th></th><th></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td></td><td>New</td><td>Old</td></tr><tr><td>K38, K50</td><td>3631950</td><td>3052820</td></tr><tr><td>QSK45, QSK60</td><td>3171769</td><td>4016438</td></tr><tr><td>* Except engines manufactured at Cummins® India Ltd.</td><td></td><td></td></tr></tbody></table></div><div class=\"callout note\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">i</span>Note · Примечание</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>This is a product improvement and not subject to campaign or TRP.</p></div></div><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/02600062.png\" alt=\"02600062.png\"></figure><p>Figure 1: New K38 and K50 Intake Valve, Part Number 3631950</p><ul><li>The new K38 and K50 Sursulf intake valve, Part Number 3631950, is a direct replacement for intake valve Part Number 3052820.</li><li>The new intake valve can be identified by the letter &#x27;O&#x27; forged into the bottom, center of the valve and by the part number laser-etched into the stem, above the collet groove. See Figure 1.</li></ul><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/02600063.png\" alt=\"02600063.png\"></figure><p>Figure 2: New QSK45 and QSK60 Intake Valve, Part Number 3171769</p><ul><li>The new QSK45 and QSK60 Sursulf intake valve, Part Number 3171769, is a direct replacement for intake valve Part Number 4016438.</li><li>The new intake valve can be identified by the letter &#x27;C&#x27; forged into the bottom, center of the valve and by the part number laser-etched into the stem, above the collet groove. See Figure 2.</li></ul>"};
